===Etymology===
{{compound|en|lock|ring}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|type of lock washer}} A textured or threaded [[washer]] used to prevent components from become loose during rotation. On bicycles they are found, for example, on a [[bottom bracket]] and a track hub.
#: {{hyper|en|lock washer}}
# {{senseid|en|ring on wheel rim for heavy equipment}} A ring (usually of steel) that is part of a [[wheel]] [[rim]] on some types of heavy equipment; it locks down the [[tire#Noun|tire]]'s mounting.

